**Proof that only the spelling changed:** I loaded the backed-up old codec under another namespace and compared it with the new one on six fixtures. It reproduces both old pins exactly. Numbering is identical on every fixture. Each new wire, respelled to the old tags and ids and rehashed, equals the old wire root and row set. The loop fixture needed its slots re-sorted after rehashing, because sets order by child ids.

**Ambiguous sites, all renamed to cursor:**
- **Pending keys:** `:yin.k/cell` becomes `:yin.k/cursor` and `:yin.k/response-cell` becomes `:yin.k/response-cursor`, because they name the census-cursor slot. This splits the vocabulary from version 2's pending maps.
- **Budget key:** `:cells` becomes `:cursors`, so a refusal now reports path `[:cursors]`. No caller passes this key.
- **Internal numbering labels:** renamed; the proof above shows numbering is unchanged.
- **Test names:** four renamed. The full list with decisions is in the report.

